# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Node.js dependencies for the CSS build (Phase 0 of the
# Bulma → DaisyUI migration). The committed CSS artifact lives
# at internal/web/static/daisyui.min.css and IS shipped; only
# the build-tooling node_modules/ is ignored.
node_modules/

# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Editor / scratch backups. Phase 6 of plans/ux-overhaul.md
# accidentally committed `fallback_renderers.go.bak` and
# `chat.js.bak`; ignore the pattern so it cannot recur.
*.bak

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Local configuration.
config.yml
config.yaml

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
.vscode/
.claude/
.continue/
.cursor/
.gemini/
.pi/
.agents/
.rules
skills-lock.json
ragabast
data/vectors
.tokensave
tmp/
**/data/vectors/

# Agent / harness instruction files. These are operator-local
# guidance for Claude / Gemini / Copilot / opencode / mise and have
# nothing to do with the ragabast build; keeping them out of the
# repo means each contributor's preferred tooling does not leak
# into the codebase.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
GEMINI.md
.github/copilot-instructions.md
opencode.json
mise.toml

# Sample / scratch data dropped under data/documents/ while
# debugging. Anything in data/ is operator-local by convention;
# only data/vectors/ is consumed at runtime (and that path is
# git-ignored above).
data/documents/

# UI review screenshots captured during the post-PR review
# passes. Always regenerated locally; never meant to live in
# the repo's history.
.review-screenshots/
